{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A feature flag resolved after the page has already painted causes a visible jump when the flagged UI swaps in — evaluate the flag before rendering, or resolve it fast enough that nothing has painted yet.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Move flag evaluation server-side, or into edge middleware, so the first HTML sent to the browser is already correct — that removes the client-side transition, and the layout shift, entirely.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Speeding up a client-side flag fetch reduces how often the shift gets noticed, it doesn't fix the coupling between flag resolution and paint — and killswitch flags that must stay live client-side need additive, non-shifting UI instead of a swap.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
